upd("n372", append="[Checked: Henry, *Quodl.* V q. 14 (Badius 1518 via SCTA) is on whether the angel knows other things by its essence, by species, or otherwise. Henry argues that cognition does not need an intelligible species impressed on the intellect (‘hoc non potest esse species intelligibilis impressa intellectui’). This fits the *responsio ad tertium* Scotus reports, but it is not a denial of ‘all intelligibility of truth’. Gorris’s description is loose (he may be compressing *speciem intelligibilem*). Reference located; the characterisation is doubtful.]", status="uncertain")
